10:02:15 settled
🟠 api in shop (prod-eu-1) keeps failing its liveness check (connection refused), so the kubelet keeps restarting it because its containers get too little time to start. Liveness gives api 40s (10s delay + 3 × 10s) but api normally needs about 75s to become ready (last 5 starts), so it is killed before it finishes starting. A startupProbe or a longer delay would let it start. The apps that use it failed soon after it changed. Fix: give the liveness probe of container app in deployment/api more time (now initialDelaySeconds 10, periodSeconds 10, failureThreshold 3). To read the output of the last crash, run kubectl logs api-8ab26137-f -c app -n shop --previous
